  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rambilash Banarsasi Yadav vs The State Of Maharashtra on 8 February, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik Diksha Rane 902. aba 177-23.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Digitally signed by Diksha Anticipatory Bail Application No.177/2023 Diksha Dinesh Dinesh Rane Rane Date: 2023.02.09 20:34:17 Rambilash Banarsasi Yadav ..Applicant +0530 Vs. The State Of Maharashtra ..Respondent ------------ Adv. Priyal Sarda i/b. Adv. Anup Lahoti for the applicant. Ms. A. A. Takalkar, App for State. Psi M. S. Bhoi, Pelhar Police Station.",
    "facts": "This is an application for pre-arrest bail in respect of First Information Report (Fir) No.837/2022 registered with the Pelhar Police Station, Nallasopara, Vasai, District-Thane under Sections 328 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (hereafter \"the Ipc\", for short) read with Sections 26(2), 4, 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. The contraband 'gutkha' and 'paan-masala' was seized from the co-accused nos.1 and 2. The co-accused no.3 was Diksha Rane 902. aba 177-23.doc to purchase the same from the co-accused nos.1 and 2 and supplied to the present applicant for further sale in Maharashtra. The 'gutkha' and 'paan-masala' has been seized. I am informed that the issue as regards the interpretation of Section 328 of the IPC is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. 5. Learned APP submitted that there are twenty-three criminal antecedents of the similar nature reported against the applicant where the applicant is a wanted accused. He has stated that on 03.10.2022, the police officers of Pelhar police station received an information that two trucks were travelling from Gujarat towards Mumbai. They were carrying banned articles namely 'Gutka'. The police officers arranged to conduct raid to intercept those trucks. At about 12.15p.m. both the trucks were intercepted. They were driven by Abhishek Nimbalkar and Kumatkar. The search of those trucks was taken. There were different bags Rambilash Banarsasi Yadav vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/194774113/ 1 containing jarda pan masala and gutka. The banned articles were worth Rs.73,41,600/-. During the investigation, name of Raghvendra Jaswant Singh transpired. He had ordered some of the goods. He gave the name of the present applicant as the person who was getting those goods from one Arjunsingh for sale in Maharashtra. These are the allegations against the present applicant.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that, there is no cogent material against the applicant. Section 328 of the I.P.C. is not attracted. The applicant is falsely implicated in this case. 3 of 3 27-aba-177-23 5. Learned APP opposed these submissions. She submitted that, the applicant has two more antecedents of a similar nature registered at Pelhar police station vide C.R.No.330 of 2021 and C.R.No.1055 of 2022.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that, there is no cogent material against the applicant. Section 328 of the I.P.C. is not attracted. The applicant is falsely implicated in this case. 3 of 3 27-aba-177-23 5. Learned APP opposed these submissions. She submitted that, the applicant has two more antecedents of a similar nature registered at Pelhar police station vide C.R.No.330 of 2021 and C.R.No.1055 of 2022.",
